# A local copy of the original game's font (commercial: never commit or ship it; the renderer uses it when it finds it)
Original-Ants/framd.ttf
Original-Ants/Franklin Gothic Medium.ttf

# The original program and local tools: keep your own copy here, never commit it. From the original game the repository
# holds only the data archive (Original-Ants/ants.chd), the maps (Original-Ants/Maps/*.LVL), the music (*.mp3, *.MID), the
# sprites and sounds decoded from the archive (asset_catalog/, and the animation table docs/chd_table4_animations.json), the front-page pictures cut out of the artwork (web/front/) and the movement tables the simulation needs (src/ants_sim/movement_tables_data.inc, generated);
# see LICENSE and "License" in the README. Ants.exe and its decompilation are local references for the reverse
# engineering (the tests and tools work without them), cnc-ddraw (ddraw.dll, ddraw.ini, the config program) and the
# libretro shaders only run the original on Windows, chat.txt is a transcript the original wrote.
Original-Ants/Ants.exe
Original-Ants/ddraw.dll
Original-Ants/ddraw.ini
Original-Ants/cnc-ddraw config.exe
Original-Ants/Shaders/
Original-Ants/chat.txt
docs/legacy/Ants.exe.c
# Local outputs of tools/analyze_binary.py (a function map and string dump of the original program: never committed)
docs/ORIGINAL_BINARY_MAP.md
docs/binary_analysis.json

# Local scratch folders and the files that editors and IDEs create inside the tree
scratch/
.cache/
compile_commands.json
.vs/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# A local run of ants_server (docs/SERVER.md: "Starting a server"): its results folder, the control secret that it makes (and the temporary files of making it), and the
# .env files of the compose examples (secrets: never commit them)
results/
control-secret
control-secret.*
.env
